    "description": "Hand-Carved Style Smoking Pipe\nChurchwarden Long Stem Design\nFaux Wood Finish, 17 Inches Long, With Box\nThis churchwarden-style smoking pipe features a characteristically long stem and an elegantly engraved bowl. The churchwarden silhouette, known for providing a cooler smoke due to the distance the smoke travels, gained historical popularity and remains a favorite for themed collections or leisurely use. This modern interpretation features a deep burgundy faux-grain finish with intricate scrollwork carvings on the bowl, capturing a vintage aesthetic.\nLong 17-inch churchwarden silhouette for a cool smoking experience\nDetailed floral and scrollwork engravings on the bowl surface\nThree-piece detachable construction including stem, bowl, and mouthpiece\nIncludes original presentation box with satin-style lining\nCondition:\nThe pipe is in excellent structural condition. The exterior finish is glossy and intact with no visible chips or deep scratches. The bowl interior appears clean and unused. The mouthpiece and stem connectors are secure. The original presentation box shows minor storage wear but remains fully intact. Warehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
